from h34 import *
M=mcq;F=tf;S=short;N=num
chapter(4,'english','the-swing','The Swing',
 ('Up in the air so blue','Robert Louis Stevenson\'s poem The Swing describes the joy of going up and down on a swing, seeing rivers, trees, cattle and the countryside from high above. In this chapter you will read the poem, learn the words pleasantest, cattle and countryside, build longer sentences step by step, learn words that can be both a noun and a verb, practise the w sound and use position words.'),
 [('What the poet feels',['The poet asks how you like to go up in a swing, up in the air so blue, and answers that it is the pleasantest thing a child can do.','The poet says the swing goes up and over the wall, high enough to see far across the countryside.','From up there the child can see rivers, trees, cattle and all, which means farm animals like cows and buffaloes.','Then the swing comes down and the child looks at the green garden and the brown roof.','The child goes flying up again, and the poem ends with the swing going up in the air and down.']),
  ('Understanding the poem',['The poet clearly enjoys swings. The lines saying it is the pleasantest thing a child can do tell us so.','The air is called blue because the sky is blue, and the child is swinging high up toward it.','The poem has a rhythm that moves up and down, just like a swing.','Rhyming words in the poem are swing and thing, and wall and all.','Words that rhyme with swing are ring, king, sing and spring.']),
  ('New words',['Pleasantest means the most enjoyable. Cattle are farm animals like cows and bulls.','Countryside is the land outside towns and cities with fields, villages and farms.']),
  ('Stringing sentences together',['We can make a sentence longer by adding details one by one.','Jeevan waited. Jeevan waited for the bus. Jeevan waited for the bus all morning. Jeevan waited for the bus all morning in the rain.','Finally: Jeevan waited for the bus all morning in the rain because his scooter was in the garage being repaired.','Each new part answers a question: for what, how long, where and why.']),
  ('Words that are both noun and verb',['Some words can be a verb in one sentence and a noun in another.','I swing on a swing. The first swing is a verb, meaning to move forward and back, and the second is a noun, an object.','The dance begins in an hour (noun). My friends and I dance when we are happy (verb).','I like to play kho-kho (verb). We will watch a play tomorrow (noun).','Can you answer the questions (verb)? I know the answer (noun). There is a fly on the wall (noun). My friends fly kites (verb).','The waves did not let us finish our sandcastle (noun). She waves to her siblings (verb).']),
  ('Sound practice and tongue twister',['A tongue twister is a sentence that is hard to say fast. How much wood would a woodchuck chuck if a woodchuck could chuck wood?','To say the w sound, make an O shape with your lips. For v, touch your upper teeth to your lower lip.','Practise: wet, wait, win, wise and white with the O shape, and vet, vine, valley, fever and fewer with the teeth on the lip.']),
  ('Position words and hobbies',['Prepositions are words used before a noun or pronoun to show place, time or direction.','On, beside, between, above, in front of, behind and under are position words.','A ladybug between two flower pots, a butterfly above a flower, a honeybee on a flower, an ant on a leaf and a caterpillar on a flowerpot are examples.','You can write a few sentences about what you enjoy in your free time, such as drawing, reading or playing kho-kho.','Draw a magical swing that can take you anywhere, like outer space or a jungle, and write about the adventure.'])],
 [('Make the sentence longer: The boy ran. Add where and why.',[('Add where: The boy ran to the park.','To the park tells where.'),('Add why: The boy ran to the park because he wanted to play.','Because gives a reason.'),('So the longer sentence is: The boy ran to the park because he wanted to play.','Each added part gives more detail.')]),
  ('Is play a noun or a verb: We will watch a play tomorrow.',[('Look at the word before play.','A play follows a.'),('A play is a story acted on a stage.','It is a thing.'),('So play is a noun here.','In I like to play it is a verb.')])],
 ('Say what the poem is about and how you can tell the poet loves swings.',['Going up and down on a swing','Seeing rivers, trees, cattle and the countryside','The pleasantest thing a child can do','Rhymes like swing and thing'],['The poet is afraid of swings','The poem is about a boat']),
 ['The poem describes the joy of swinging high above the countryside.','Pleasantest means most enjoyable; cattle are farm animals.','A sentence can be made longer by adding details.','Some words, like play, dance and fly, can be nouns or verbs.','Position words like above, between and under show where things are.'],
 [M('1',1,'What does the poet see when the swing goes over the wall?','Rivers, trees and cattle',[('Mountains and snow','Rivers and trees'),('The sea and ships','Rivers and trees')],'He sees the countryside.'),
  M('2',1,'Does the poet enjoy swings?','Yes, he calls it the pleasantest thing',[('No, he is afraid','He enjoys it'),('He never goes on one','He goes on it')],'The poet loves it.'),
  M('3',1,'Why is the air called blue?','Because the sky is blue',[('Because it is cold','It is the sky'),('Because it is dirty','It is the sky')],'The swing goes high up in the blue sky.'),
  M('4',2,'What does pleasantest mean?','Most enjoyable',[('Most scary','Not the meaning'),('Most boring','Not the meaning')],'Pleasantest means very enjoyable.'),
  M('5',2,'What are cattle?','Farm animals like cows',[('Wild birds','Not the meaning'),('Fruits','Not the meaning')],'Cattle are cows and bulls.'),
  M('6',2,'Which word rhymes with swing?','Thing',[('Wall','Different sound'),('Blue','Different sound')],'Swing and thing rhyme.'),
  M('7',2,'In I swing on a swing, the second swing is a ___.','noun',[('verb','The first swing is the verb'),('adjective','Not the meaning')],'It names an object.'),
  M('8',2,'In My friends fly kites, fly is a ___.','verb',[('noun','Fly is the action here'),('adjective','Not the meaning')],'It shows an action.'),
  M('9',2,'In There is a fly on the wall, fly is a ___.','noun',[('verb','It names an insect'),('adverb','Not the meaning')],'It names an insect.'),
  M('10',2,'Which is a position word?','between',[('swing','A noun or verb'),('happy','An adjective')],'Between shows where something is.'),
  F('11',2,'A tongue twister is hard to say fast.',True,'That is why it is called a twister.'),
  S('12',3,'Who wrote the poem The Swing?',['robert louis stevenson','stevenson','r l stevenson'],'The poem is by Robert Louis Stevenson.')],
 keep=['swing','cattle'])
